{"Title":"An Act relative to protecting local retirees","BillNumber":"S1662","DocketNumber":"SD719","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PRF0","Name":"Paul R. Feeney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PRF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T11:20:32.583"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PRF0","Name":"Paul R. Feeney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PRF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T11:20:32.5833333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1662/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Feeney, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1662) of Paul R. Feeney for legislation to protect local retirees.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 9E of Chapter 32B of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following sentence:- \r\n\tIn the event that the governmental unit approves an increase in the percent of the premium to be contributed by its retired employees, the percent of premium being paid by a retired employee at that time will not be increased to the higher percent.\r\n\tSECTION 2. The provisions of this act shall take effect on January 1, 2023.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}